This engine includes and locally modifies the following third-party library:

  github.com/librespeed/speedtest-cli v1.0.14
  Upstream tag: v1.0.14
  Upstream commit: 42e5f76c90e64e04ab7079fd76d833dfe41805da
  Source: https://github.com/librespeed/speedtest-cli/tree/v1.0.14
  License: GNU Lesser General Public License v3

The full upstream license and incorporated GPL terms are included as
LGPL-3.0.txt and GPL-3.0.txt. The unmodified vendored upstream LICENSE is
retained at vendor/github.com/librespeed/speedtest-cli/LICENSE. Other vendored
dependencies retain their upstream license files under vendor/.

Local fork changes are limited to vendor/github.com/librespeed/speedtest-cli/defs:

  adapter.go       Context-aware transfer adapter, 500 ms progress callbacks,
                   HTTP response validation, shared byte budget, and upload
                   accounting only after successful full-body consumption.
  bytes_counter.go Public atomic byte commit used for confirmed uploads.
  server.go       Per-run HTTP client/referer injection and a cancellable HTTP
                   ping method with HTTP status/body validation.

These changes exist because the CLI worker requires cancellation, cookie-jar
and direct-DNS transport injection, bounded traffic, observable real progress,
and successful application-level HTTP confirmation. The repeated parallel
request model and average-rate counter remain from the upstream LibreSpeed
implementation. Local changes and the upstream source are available in this
source tree. Re-generating vendor from go.mod replaces the fork; reapply and
retest these narrowly scoped changes if upgrading.

The engine application is linked with the modified LGPL library. Build it with
`go build -mod=vendor`; the corresponding source is the complete `engine/`
directory. Keep that source, LGPL-3.0.txt, GPL-3.0.txt, this notice and the
relink permissions/terms with any binary distribution.
